Phase 1:
In this phase, I created a Song class and a SinglyLinkedList that can add songs to the end and display the playlist.
A linked list stores elements in separate nodes that point to the next node, while an array stores elements in consecutive positions in memory.
This means a linked list connects its elements using references instead of relying on indexes.

Phase 2:
In this phase, I implemented the Iterable interface and added a custom iterator with a remove() method to delete songs from the playlist.
Unlinking a node updates the next pointer of the previous node to bypass the target element and point straight to the current node.
This allows the iterator to securely delete items while keeping its place in the list via the already-advanced cursor.
